=3D"color:transparent" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/images/courses/coding-=
patterns/backtracking/find-all-permutations/image-14-01-1-E2CNBZ26.svg?dpl=
=3Ddpl_CEjisbLnWxFQGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c"></div></figure>
<hr>
<p>Now that we've found one permutation, let's <em>backtrack</em> to find o=
thers. Start by removing the most recently added number, 6, bringing us bac=
k to [4, 5]:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
